WEBVTT

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.820
Is this your first time at the carpentry guild, Hakumei?

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.240
Yep. It's huge.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.410
Let's go in. Try not to freak out, yeah?

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.370
I-I'll be okay.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:29.590
Everything's massive.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.960
Ain't it?

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.800
Mr. President. Mr. Vice President.
Good morning to you both.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.640
Oh, Iwashi. I see you're as short as ever.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.770
No, you're just big, sir.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.850
He's huge!

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.190
Oh? You must be... Um...

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.190
Hakumei, right?

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.610
That's the guild president. It figures he'd know the name of anyone in his trade, right?

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.120
O-Oh yeah.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.120
Nice to meet you.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.170
I'm Narai. So, what brings you here, Hakumei?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.020
I want to help the guild on the stone wall repair project.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.030
No.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.240
Why not?!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.860
Simmer down.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:03.320
Sorry for her lack o' manners, Mr. President.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.290
I can handle anything you throw at me!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.750
Surveying, drafting, backfilling, selecting the stones...

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.630
I can handle all of that myself.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:15.590
Go home.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.670
Then, let me cook!

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.130
We bring our own food.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.380
I can put up scaffolding!

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.300
We've got that covered.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.340
Tool maintenance?

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.220
We all manage our own tools.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:32.440
Whenever I made my way down that cobbled street,

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.900
it always struck me how beautiful the wall was.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.190
I'm sorry.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.080
We'll be heading back out.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:46.990
Right.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.000
C'mon, Hakumei.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.130
Sorry for wasting your time.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.130
Don't get yourself down like that.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.840
I'm not feeling down. Are you
going off to fix the stone wall?

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:06.930
Yeah.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.430
Boss!

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.690
Huh?!

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.320
Tools are a craftsman's life.
I know it's asking a lot, but...

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:21.940
Even if it's just washing the mud off of them,
will you please let me help you?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.070
<i>Just</i> washing the mud off?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.830
These tools are <i>way</i> bigger than what you work with.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.870
I know that.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.960
They're about as big as you are.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.250
That's fine.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.250
<i>And</i> they're sharp.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.460
I can handle it!

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.170
I'm leavin' the repair and the sharpening to you.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.010
Thank you, Iwashi!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.260
Q-Quit it with the tail!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.730
And what happened to calling me boss?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:06.110
We're in the middle of repairing the damage caused by the landslide.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:09.160
When this is done, the big stone can go back to where it was.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.410
It got hit real bad.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.040
It may not look it, but we've fixed up quite a bit already.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.750
Hakumei.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.500
I thought we might see you here.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.180
I won't get involved with any construction. I promise.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.050
Katen, lift me up to the far right.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:30.890
Okay.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.020
Listen up, you louts! We're back at it today!

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.780
The Borestone Guild stands for...

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:44.780
Safety!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.700
Speed!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:46.780
Thoroughness!

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.660
Camaraderie!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.160
Okay. Time to head up to work.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.460
Watch the president at work.
You might learn a thing or two.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.300
Guess there was no need to say anything.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.060
These roots sure aren't making my life easy.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.400
Here, wash and sharpen these for me.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.270
No problem.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.070
And this sickle too, if you please.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.700
Sure thing. No need to hold back.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:34.160
Don't cut yourself.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.620
Didn't I say I could handle it?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.500
Hey, Katen, pass me the rope for leveling.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:43.670
Certainly.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.260
Mr. President, Mr. Vice President,
I'm leaving for the day.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.760
Good work today.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.850
See you again tomorrow.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.270
Quitting time, Hakumei.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.860
Okay. Just one more left.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.900
Sir.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.900
You're pretty good.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.860
But there's a better way to hold the whetstone.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.530
For sickles, hold it like this. Fingers pointing out.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.620
Your hands are so big that I don't get it...

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.040
Like this?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.460
No, no.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.330
Like this?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.290
Hmm, still a bit off.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.670
Not heading home yet?
How about this?

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.000
That's it!
Not heading home yet?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:26.590
That's it!

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.380
The leader always leaves last.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:35.300
Plus, it would be lonely to walk home alone.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.350
Uh, sure...

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.530
Oh! Welcome home.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.740
I'm baaack...

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.950
Hungry, are we?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.530
So, how was the worksite?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.910
They're running such a tight ship
that I can't really fit myself in.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:09.590
Well, you'll just have to do what you can, right?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.130
That's right.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:46.170
Hey, you're looking kinda sleepy. You all right?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:49.550
I'm fine. Is the president here?

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:50.960
He's right over there.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.300
Sir.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.010
What is it, Hakumei?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.930
Could you look at this?

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.850
I made it yesterday.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.770
I charted the sizes and cuts of rocks that would match up with the areas under construction—

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:08.860
Hey.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.480
Exactly when did you make this?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.490
L-Last night...

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.240
Stay off the site when you haven't slept properly.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.870
Go home and get some rest.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.080
I'm going to go draw some water.
Want to come help me?

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.290
No, I can't.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.510
You and the president are keeping this worksite running smoothly, right?

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:39.430
Please don't worry about me.
Do what you need to do.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.720
Okay, understood.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.520
Thanks.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:48.440
And on that note, excuse me, Iwashi.
I'll do double the sharpening tomorrow.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.730
Sure thing. See you tomorrow.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.030
She's really something, isn't she?

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.320
Yes, quite.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.620
I'm home...

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:09.880
Huh? Hakumei? You're home already?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.880
She's asleep...

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.890
All the knives are sharpened.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.150
The Borestone Guild stands for...

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.900
Safety! Speed! Thoroughness!

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.820
Camaraderie!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.790
You've gotten quicker at sharpening the tools, eh?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.300
I had to with huge blades like these!

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:58.170
Right now, the kitchen knives' edges are about as thin as paper.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.180
Pretty impressive.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.680
Hakumei.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.100
Mr. President...

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.310
I've got a favor to ask.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.060
This is my chisel. Can you sharpen it for me?

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:16.070
Huh?

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.490
Well, I don't think... I mean...

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:20.450
What's the problem?

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.570
Didn't you say you could handle anything I threw at you?

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.700
So what is it, then?

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.540
Is it because it's my chisel?

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.880
S-Sorry. I just can't.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:37.840
Why not?

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:44.470
Iwashi put his tools, the life of a carpenter,
in my care because he trusts me.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:48.470
So I'm sharpening them as if my life depends on it.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.690
But I can't sharpen yours. It's still scary.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.480
You two are good friends, aren't you?

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:02.860
Show up in work clothes starting tomorrow.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.620
Y-You mean I can join the repair work, right?

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.370
Yeah.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.500
Did you hear that, Iwashi?

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:16.090
Yeah, that's great. Careful not to slack off, now.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.300
Yahoo!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.420
I told you to quit it with the tail! Leggo!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.680
You're a kind one, Narai.
I told you to quit it with the tail! Leggo!

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.050
I told you to quit it with the tail! Leggo!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:25.760
I can't rely on someone who fears nothing.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.140
Lemme go! I said quit! Quit it!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.890
Oh, and Hakumei...

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.230
Have a work coat made as well.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:37.230
You have a wife too, don't you? "Mikochi," was it?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.070
Er...

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.360
I'm a woman, you know.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.030
Sorry.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.040
Heave ho!

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.750
Just a bit more! Go!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.340
Heave ho!

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.510
How's it look, Hakumei?

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.130
Almost there!

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:05.880
<i>You're... doing repairs, right?</i>

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.140
Mikochi-san?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.680
Coming!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:16.020
Sorry for making you help me with the food, Mikochi-san.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.560
Oh, it's fine.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.320
Look at how my husband's pushing his crew right now.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:20.730
Iwashi! Put your back into it!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.820
As the day drags on,
everyone ends up dead on their feet.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:23.570
Yessir.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:26.860
So I have to at least make sure that they eat when that happens.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.320
I see.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.200
Hakuyo-neesan.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.540
Let me have a little snack before lunch.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.500
Katen-chan.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:39.920
I'd get out of here before Narai loses his temper, if I were you.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.130
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.170
I brought up some joint stones.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.170
Good.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.720
Hey, Hakumei.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.510
Can you install joint stones?

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:57.100
That's where you wedge a flat rock under a shaky stone, right?

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.560
Whoa.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.030
A nice, smooth ride to the top, huh?

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.360
You'll get used to it.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.450
Here you go. Right there.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.990
This is the face of the stone wall. The largest stone.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:16.250
There's no replacement available for a stone this size. Anchor it properly.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.040
Iwashi, come over and help her!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:19.750
Yessir!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.130
It isn't really that hard of a job.
Nothing to stress over.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.100
If the president tells you not to stress...

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.850
...it's just gonna make you <i>more</i> nervous, right?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.520
Well, do your best.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.030
Right.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.400
How is it, Hakumei?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.660
It's a tight squeeze. I'm driving it in, so hold it steady.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:53.410
Gotcha.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.080
Vice-president!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.040
Let me hop on again!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.670
What happened?

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.300
The sound it made felt wrong.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.880
There's no one below, is there?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:10.300
What's going on?

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.800
Iwashi, get on!
What's going on?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.800
Hurry! Hurry!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:13.930
Okay...

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.110
Oh my word...

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.440
So it really was ready to shatter.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.400
It was a good drainage outlet,
and it's in direct sunlight.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.360
Just wore out with age, I suppose.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.080
Are you hurt?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.160
No, I'm okay.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.290
I should have checked more carefully. I'm sorry.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.340
Don't... worry about it...

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.800
Let's take a short break.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.800
There's plenty more where that came from!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:55.760
Thanks!

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:00.730
Watery food's good to replenish the sweat I've lost,
but I wish I had more salt and oil too.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:02.850
Oh, in that case...

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.150
Here's some salt-roasted watermelon seeds.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.610
What?

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.280
Chock-full of protein and fats.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.490
Hakuyo-san told me that.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.660
As expected from a carpenter's wife.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.330
What are they doing?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.660
Having a staring contest with the blueprints.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.170
They lost the face of the stone wall.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.920
Maybe they'll put us on hold to dig up more rocks.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:32.050
There was a huge boulder around the entrance to the road, wasn't there?

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.470
Can't we use that?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:40.310
Oh, that one's just too big. And it's so hard that we wouldn't even be able to chisel away at it.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.980
Okay, let me try something!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.650
Sir.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.570
What is it, Hakumei?

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.320
I've got an idea!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.200
So basically...

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.570
First apply a burn to the right area,

00:16:55.570 --> 00:17:00.580
then do a rapid cooldown with ice water to make a fracture.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:04.750
And then, in order to not break more off than we need to,

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.330
we'll use your chisel to finish splitting it.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.750
What will we use to make it burn for so long?

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:16.430
Crush the watermelon seeds and knead them into pine oil to make some solid fuel.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:20.260
I see. That might work.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.100
Right?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.140
Okay. Gather up the tools you'll need.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.770
All right, here goes!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:27.520
Wait, Hakumei.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.480
Take this.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.780
This time, it's a serious request.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.660
Hakumei-san!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.790
Oh, you're the president's wife.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:46.830
Thank you for earlier. He's actually quite a coward when it comes to things like that.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:47.370
Huh?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:51.000
The mistake he made giving you that order really shook him up.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.090
Thanks to you, he's ready to take charge again.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.130
Is... that so?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.760
Of course!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:02.600
He's very fussy about his tools. Best of luck!

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:03.430
Thanks.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:28.870
Pine oil and crushed watermelon seeds.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.500
Mix them together...

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.500
Looks like it's got a nice texture.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:38.970
Now, we'll just let the foremen work out the best burn line.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:43.140
Is figuring that out pretty difficult, then?

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:48.390
Yeah. If it's even a little off, the chisel might go any which way when you drive it in.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:51.270
You need someone experienced to get it right.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:58.400
The grain of the stone is irrelevant.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:01.410
The chisel.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.200
Here it is.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.160
Thanks.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.670
This is fine work.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.170
Thank you.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.430
All right... One clean strike.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.070
It split!

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:42.660
Never doubted you, boss!

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:43.950
Naturally.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.660
I'll put the joint stone in once we get this thing up.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.370
Then we'll all be done!

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.040
Sir!

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:55.290
I can do the joint stone.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.750
There's not much scaffolding to speak of up there.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.090
I-I can still...

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.050
Whoa!

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:03.340
Why don't you two do it together?

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.850
Hakuyo...

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.640
But it just collapsed a little while ago.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.100
Narai.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.140
Were you listening?

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.820
Could you give me a hand, Hakumei?

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.110
Sure.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.240
Your wife sure is scary.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.450
You could say that.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:36.420
Listen up, Hakumei. You're going to drive the joint stone in horizontally.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.670
If you drive it in too far, it'll just make it less stable.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.760
Understood.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:49.510
The boulder here... it almost collapsed once before.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:53.730
Katen and I repaired it ourselves.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:21:00.400
People can't enjoy the walkway if there's a teetering boulder like that.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.740
When the big stone settled,
pedestrians filled the street again,

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.620
and before we realized it,
everyone had given the stone a name.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:08.700
Surprised you earlier, huh?
and before we realized it,
everyone had given the stone a name.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.040
and before we realized it,
everyone had given the stone a name.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:14.080
It looked like the stone was boring through the gravel around it.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.210
The Borestone.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:22.050
So that was the beginning of the Borestone Guild?

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:26.760
But Katen and Hakuyo called it by a different name.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:31.560
Narai Rock. Hah.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:36.940
That's a story from long ago.
A new rock needs a new name.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.480
Narai Rock is still a good name, I'd say.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:42.360
You reckon?

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:51.830
Well, then. To celebrate the repair of the stone wall, here's a word from our president.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:57.580
Starting tomorrow, this'll be a road again.
But tonight it's our own personal party grounds!

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.340
Hakumei, do the drill!

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.960
Here goes!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:05.340
Everyone, what does the Borestone Guild stand for?!

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:10.720
Safety, Speed, Thoroughness, Camaraderie!

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:16.600
Have some more.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:18.100
Here you go!

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:35.450
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:43.250
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:47.260
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:51.220
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:55.770
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.150
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:03.770
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:07.490
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:11.410
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:16.240
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:20.210
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:24.170
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:29.470
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:33.010
At least, that's how we're feeling
